 S~S  Release notes version 260212: app-events repository activity: create the repository

------------------------------------------

    Instantiate the repository version control database from file system version control database.

------------------------------------------

    This first version in the repository of the app-event SimpleSal App does not work.

    The reason it does not work is due to a simple configuration error that may be common when
    developers port their App into a SimpleSal App.  The release with the change to the software
    to fix the configuration error will follow (soon) and the repository Application may be
    explored by the developer by comparing the early nonworking version with the working version.

    Any repository has the ability to manage even single-letter changes to source files.

    The intention is to demonstrate the hidden complexities within ssTEA that support the main
    educational goal.  Extensive explanatory messages are enabled in the failing version simply
    to show how the explanatory messages communicate the condition of the App to the developer.

    The change from nonworking to working will eliminate many of the messages during init State;
    then the periodic display of the ssTEA API information for each Event will pop some eyeballs.

    The App with messages fully enabled may hide the signal for the serial port each period.

    The 1-second output to the serial port shows Time progressing, the Built-In LED is turned ON
    at the start of a 5-second period, and then an Event occurs 3 seconds later to turn it OFF.

